  "title": "Jobs join the caller's inbound distributed trace",
  "summary": "When OTEL tracing is enabled, a job run through a webhook or REST endpoint with a W3C traceparent header is connected to the caller's distributed trace. The job span and its flow step and script spans are relocated under the caller's span so the whole execution appears as one end-to-end trace, instead of as a separate one.",
